WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:07.407
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:14.248
Yeah, I'm feeling pretty good
right about now.

00:00:15.115 --> 00:00:16.316
G-MAN: Rise and shine, Mr. Freeman.

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:18.986
BLAAAGH!
G-MAN: Rise and shine, Mr. Freeman.

00:00:18.986 --> 00:00:21.421
G-MAN: Rise and shine.

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:23.156
Back the fuck up!

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:25.225
G-MAN: Not that I wish to imply

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:28.195
Back it up! Keep going!
G-MAN: you have been sleeping on the job.

00:00:28.195 --> 00:00:30.163
AAAAAH!
G-MAN: No one has been more deserving

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:31.498
Stop...
G-MAN: of a rest,

00:00:31.498 --> 00:00:33.800
G-MAN: and all the effort in the world

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.536
Just stop...
G-MAN: would have gone to waste until...

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:38.138
Your breath smells like paint.

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:42.976
G-MAN: Well, let's just say
your hour has... come again.

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:46.346
That's close enough! Personal space!

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:48.782
PERSONAL SPACE, YOU FREAK!

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:49.816
Aaaargh!

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:55.856
G-MAN: The right man in the wrong place
can make all the difference in the world.

00:00:55.856 --> 00:00:57.357
Oh, who said that? JFK?

00:00:57.357 --> 00:01:00.227
G-MAN: So wake up, Mr. Freeman.

00:01:00.227 --> 00:01:01.461
Maybe Churchill.

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:04.364
G-MAN: Wake up and smell the ashes.

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:07.067
Yeah, bye! Don't let me keep you!

00:01:08.335 --> 00:01:11.605
Oh, god! Is he gone? Am I on Earth again?

00:01:11.605 --> 00:01:13.574
Good! Well, I'm not going back.

00:01:13.574 --> 00:01:15.342
YOU HEAR ME?! I'M NOT GOING BACK!

00:01:15.342 --> 00:01:16.276
MAN #1: I didn't see you get on.

00:01:16.276 --> 00:01:17.711
Yeah, where are we?

00:01:17.711 --> 00:01:22.282
This is Hawaii, right? That was the
deal! He was going to send me to Hawaii.

00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:24.818
This doesn't look like Hawaii.

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:26.987
Does Hawaii have a railway?

00:01:26.987 --> 00:01:28.622
I think they do.

00:01:28.622 --> 00:01:29.556
Aloha!

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:32.826
MAN #2: No matter how many times I've
been relocated, I never get used to it.

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:36.663
Okay, you're going to be a
crappy wingman. No bars for you.

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:39.900
I guess this is the main island.

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:40.901
MAN #1: End of the line.

00:01:40.901 --> 00:01:42.402
Could be Oahu.

00:01:42.402 --> 00:01:45.772
Okay, no greeters. This kind of sucks.

00:01:46.073 --> 00:01:49.042
WAAAAGH! I'M BLIND! I CAN'T SEE!

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:50.577
HELP! HELP ME!

00:01:50.577 --> 00:01:54.414
NO! Bl-BLAAGH! WHAT WAS THAT?!

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:56.183
I should've come by boat.

00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:58.752
There's a lot of trash here.

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:02.522
I'm confused. What is this?

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:04.424
ADMINISTRATOR: ...in the Citadel
so thoughtfully provided...

00:02:04.424 --> 00:02:06.960
This is like Max Headroom for old people.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:10.230
ADMINISTRATOR: I've been proud
to call City 17 my home...

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:12.099
Oh, it's a timeshare infomercial.

00:02:12.099 --> 00:02:13.634
ADMINISTRATOR: Whether you are
here to stay, or...

00:02:13.634 --> 00:02:16.703
Or traveler's insurance or some crap.

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:19.239
Oh! Am I seeing things?

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:21.308
No!

00:02:22.476 --> 00:02:25.145
Oh, this is perfect!

00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:29.850
Yeah, keep sweeping, zapface! You've
got a lot of work ahead of you!

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:34.554
Oh, this makes my day. Next to
seeing their heads on a stick,

00:02:34.554 --> 00:02:38.925
this is about the best thing I could've
asked for. I'm going to like this.

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:42.496
Knowing that we've domesticated
those things gives me some real hope.

00:02:42.496 --> 00:02:43.063
METROCOP #1: Move away.

00:02:43.063 --> 00:02:44.931
MAN #3: But this stuff... it's
all I have left.

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:45.298
MAN #3: Oof!

00:02:45.298 --> 00:02:47.167
Oh, here we go!

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:48.268
MAN #3: All right. I'm moving! Jesus.

00:02:48.268 --> 00:02:49.970
Awww...

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:54.141
I could watch cop fights all
day. Never gets old.

00:02:54.141 --> 00:02:55.575
WOMAN #1: Were you the only ones
on that train?

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:59.746
More trash...  Uh... What?

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:01.948
Oh, yeah. It was just me.

00:03:01.948 --> 00:03:03.884
It's always just me.

00:03:03.884 --> 00:03:06.386
Hey, I get why there's so much trash.

00:03:06.386 --> 00:03:09.089
They're leaving it for
the alien to sweep up!

00:03:09.089 --> 00:03:12.926
Yeah, look at that. Nobody's even trying.

00:03:12.926 --> 00:03:17.397
And you know what?
I don't blame you one bit.

00:03:17.397 --> 00:03:21.668
MAN #4: Don't drink the water! They put
something in it... to make you forget.

00:03:21.668 --> 00:03:23.103
MAN #4: I don't even
remember how I got here.

00:03:23.103 --> 00:03:25.972
Hey! I don't either! What's going on?

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:28.742
Okay, I remember fighting an elder god,

00:03:28.742 --> 00:03:31.411
I won because I'm that good,

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:36.283
then some lights flash, the CIA
spook made a deal, now I'm here.

00:03:36.283 --> 00:03:39.986
Y'know, Time Lord or not, I think
he might be a sexual predator.

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:42.389
He had me completely paralyzed,

00:03:42.389 --> 00:03:45.258
and I swear to God, I thought he
was going to French kiss me.

00:03:45.258 --> 00:03:48.495
That was hell. That was absolute hell.

00:03:48.495 --> 00:03:50.730
Hey, why is everyone wearing the
same clothes?

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.265
MAN #5: I'm working up the nerve to go on.

00:03:52.265 --> 00:03:54.401
Is this a work camp or something?

00:03:54.401 --> 00:03:56.203
Did he send me to prison?

00:03:56.203 --> 00:03:57.504
Why would he do that?

00:03:57.504 --> 00:04:01.074
If he wanted me dead, he could've
just left me where I was,

00:04:01.074 --> 00:04:03.777
but he recruited me, so what's my mission?

00:04:03.777 --> 00:04:05.045
I don't know these people.

00:04:05.045 --> 00:04:06.646
I think I'm in the future.

00:04:06.646 --> 00:04:09.916
That alien didn't get a job
sweeping overnight.

00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:13.286
Oh, great. I don't even have my
ID. This is going to go well.

00:04:13.854 --> 00:04:14.588
Yep.

00:04:14.588 --> 00:04:16.423
All right. Uh...

00:04:16.423 --> 00:04:19.359
Hi. I'm a political refugee seeking asylum.

00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:20.660
My government betrayed me.

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:22.362
METROCOP #2: You! Citizen! Come with me.

00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:27.134
Yes! Citizen! Exactly! I am a citizen!

00:04:27.134 --> 00:04:29.336
Now we're getting somewhere.

00:04:29.336 --> 00:04:30.871
MAN #6: This must be a mistake.

00:04:30.871 --> 00:04:33.940
MAN #6: I got a standard relocation
coupon just like everybody else.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:38.211
Oh yeah. Argue with bureaucracy.
Good luck with that.

00:04:38.211 --> 00:04:41.982
Hey, I don't have an ID, but you can look
me up by Social Security number, right?

00:04:41.982 --> 00:04:42.582
METROCOP #2: GET IN!

00:04:42.582 --> 00:04:43.950
Yeah, yeah.

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:47.487
Oh, what the hell is this? You
do dental work here, too?

00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:48.388
METROCOP #3: Need any help with this one?

00:04:48.388 --> 00:04:49.322
METROCOP #2: No, I'm good.

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:51.191
The chair doesn't have any restraints.

00:04:51.191 --> 00:04:51.958
METROCOP #2: Back up!

00:04:51.958 --> 00:04:54.828
You'd get yourself killed trying
to torture somebody in this.

00:04:54.828 --> 00:04:57.864
METROCOP #2: Yeah. I'm gonna
need me some privacy for this!

00:04:57.864 --> 00:04:59.566
Okay! Guess I'm wrong!

00:04:59.566 --> 00:05:00.367
METROCOP #2: Now...

00:05:00.367 --> 00:05:02.569
I'll play dumb, then bash him
as hard as I can.

00:05:02.569 --> 00:05:04.571
BARNEY: ...about that beer I owed ya.

00:05:04.571 --> 00:05:05.138
What?

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:07.808
BARNEY: It's me, Gordon,
Barney from Black Mesa.

00:05:07.808 --> 00:05:08.975
Not ringing a bell.

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:11.511
BARNEY: Sorry for the scare, I had
to put on a show for the cameras.

00:05:11.511 --> 00:05:14.147
BARNEY: I've been working
undercover with Civil Protection.

00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:15.949
BARNEY: I can't take too long or
they'll get suspicious.

00:05:15.949 --> 00:05:18.618
BARNEY: I'm WAY behind on my beating quota.

00:05:18.618 --> 00:05:19.286
Pervert.

00:05:19.286 --> 00:05:21.154
KLEINER: Yes, Barney. What is it?

00:05:21.154 --> 00:05:21.988
Oh, it's Kleiner.

00:05:21.988 --> 00:05:23.924
KLEINER: I'm in the middle
of a critical test.

00:05:23.924 --> 00:05:26.259
BARNEY: Sorry, doc, but look who's here.

00:05:26.259 --> 00:05:26.860
Yo!

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:30.063
KLEINER: Great Scott! Gordon Freeman!

00:05:30.063 --> 00:05:30.864
You know it!

00:05:30.864 --> 00:05:31.898
KLEINER: I would've expected more warning.

00:05:31.898 --> 00:05:33.667
BARNEY: Yeah, you and me both, doc.

00:05:33.667 --> 00:05:36.636
BARNEY: He was about to board
the express to Nova Prospekt.

00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:39.206
KLEINER: Well, Barney, what do you intend?

00:05:39.206 --> 00:05:40.840
BARNEY: I'm thinking, I'm thinking!

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:43.643
KLEINER: Alyx is around here... somewhere.

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:46.379
KLEINER: She would have a better
idea of how to get him here.

00:05:46.379 --> 00:05:49.983
BARNEY: Well, as long as he stays away
from checkpoints, we should be okay.

00:05:49.983 --> 00:05:50.417
What?

00:05:50.417 --> 00:05:52.786
BARNEY: Listen, I gotta go, doc.
We're taking enough chances as it is.

00:05:52.786 --> 00:05:55.322
I don't know what's going on, guys.

00:05:55.322 --> 00:05:57.424
KLEINER: Gordon, good to see you.

00:05:57.424 --> 00:05:58.225
Respect!

00:05:58.225 --> 00:06:02.128
BARNEY: Okay, Gordon. You're gonna have to
make your own way to Doctor Kleiner's lab.

00:06:02.128 --> 00:06:03.163
I need an address.

00:06:03.163 --> 00:06:04.497
[knocking]
BARNEY: Oh, man! That's what I was afraid of.

00:06:04.497 --> 00:06:05.966
Blah!
BARNEY: Get in here, Gordon,

00:06:05.966 --> 00:06:07.334
BARNEY: before you blow my cover.

00:06:07.334 --> 00:06:08.902
Okay! Fine!

00:06:08.902 --> 00:06:11.838
I don't even know what's happening.
I don't care if you get fired.

00:06:11.838 --> 00:06:14.841
BARNEY: Get through that window and
keep going until you're in the plaza.

00:06:14.841 --> 00:06:16.409
BARNEY: I'll meet up with you later.

00:06:17.177 --> 00:06:20.947
So that's Kleiner's errand boy.
This makes more sense now.

00:06:20.947 --> 00:06:25.785
Hmm. Well, I trust Kleiner... and
that's about the whole list, so...

00:06:28.655 --> 00:06:30.156
Yeah, all right...

00:06:31.758 --> 00:06:33.627
RAAAAAAGH!

00:06:33.627 --> 00:06:37.097
I can only assume there's a
reason for doing this.

00:06:37.097 --> 00:06:40.600
I'm too confused to know if I
have problems or not.

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:43.103
So, why is Kleiner in Hawaii?

00:06:43.103 --> 00:06:45.105
He's probably in one of the observatories

00:06:45.105 --> 00:06:47.674
trying to pinpoint where the
aliens came from.

00:06:47.674 --> 00:06:50.043
Did the CIA grab him, too?

00:06:50.043 --> 00:06:51.311
METROCOP #4: Pick up that can.

00:06:51.311 --> 00:06:54.047
Oh! Is this what I think it is?

00:06:54.047 --> 00:06:56.616
METROCOP #4: Now.
Put it... in the trash can.

00:06:56.616 --> 00:07:00.854
Ah! I see my reputation precedes me!

00:07:00.854 --> 00:07:02.022
All right.

00:07:02.022 --> 00:07:04.190
How about from here? This is good.

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:05.325
Easy.

00:07:05.325 --> 00:07:07.527
METROCOP #4: All right. You can
go. Heh heh...

00:07:07.527 --> 00:07:10.196
You know how many sodas I drank in college?

00:07:10.196 --> 00:07:12.098
Seriously, I'm the master.

00:07:12.098 --> 00:07:14.501
Hey, was that on camera? No...

00:07:14.501 --> 00:07:18.204
I could've made that shot
blindfolded. I'm not even joking.

00:07:18.204 --> 00:07:20.674
I've thrown thousands of soda cans.

00:07:20.674 --> 00:07:23.843
I got my degree under the
tutelage of Dr. Pepper.

00:07:23.843 --> 00:07:25.412
Oh, a food line.

00:07:25.412 --> 00:07:28.148
Well, I don't have an ID so that's out.

00:07:28.148 --> 00:07:31.151
I'll just steal something later.
There's too many cops here.

00:07:31.151 --> 00:07:33.753
It's best to grab it out of
somebody's hand on the street

00:07:33.753 --> 00:07:37.891
because they'll chase you, but they won't
file a report over a stolen hot dog.

00:07:37.891 --> 00:07:42.228
Ooookaaay... this is definitely not Hawaii.

00:07:42.228 --> 00:07:45.365
Yeah, they fucked me. The CIA fucked me.

00:07:45.365 --> 00:07:50.270
What's that lettering? Is this
Russia? Eastern Europe? Dammit.

00:07:50.270 --> 00:07:55.075
So I have no money, no ID, and
I'm lost in another country.

00:07:55.075 --> 00:07:57.744
What a great plan this was.

00:07:57.744 --> 00:08:01.414
Well, I'm just going to have to
hustle my way out of this.

00:08:01.414 --> 00:08:03.216
Yeah, you'll do.

00:08:03.216 --> 00:08:04.150
A-ahem.

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:06.019
Hey, girl! How you doin'?

00:08:06.019 --> 00:08:08.154
WOMAN #2: If I talk to you out
here, we'll both be in trouble.

00:08:08.154 --> 00:08:10.890
What the hell? What's going on?

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:12.859
Desperate women love me.

00:08:12.859 --> 00:08:14.728
[sighs]

00:08:14.728 --> 00:08:16.963
This is a complete shit show.

00:08:16.963 --> 00:08:20.567
The CIA creep said he had an
important job for me.

00:08:20.567 --> 00:08:24.771
You know what would've helped?
Knowing what my job is?

00:08:24.771 --> 00:08:27.073
What's this? A Gestapo raid?

00:08:27.073 --> 00:08:30.410
Yeah! Great place to drop me
with no information!

00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:32.879
I'm surprised he didn't send me here naked.

00:08:32.879 --> 00:08:33.847
[thumping] That really would--

00:08:33.847 --> 00:08:35.315
[thumping]

00:08:35.315 --> 00:08:37.183
[thumping] Oh my god. It's a Tripod.

00:08:37.183 --> 00:08:38.785
It's a fucking Tripod!

00:08:38.785 --> 00:08:40.920
Uh... I gotta get out of here.

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:43.923
They're real! How did we-- No,
I'll figure it out later.

00:08:43.923 --> 00:08:47.093
I've gotta hide. This explains a lot.

00:08:47.093 --> 00:08:48.895
Well, they're not Capping me.

00:08:48.895 --> 00:08:52.499
I'll kill everyone in this city
before I let that happen.

00:08:52.499 --> 00:08:53.933
Tripods...

00:08:53.933 --> 00:08:57.804
That must be where these friggin'
servo-skulls came from, too.

00:08:57.804 --> 00:08:59.472
Everything's changed.

00:08:59.472 --> 00:09:02.308
Hey, are you two Capped? How do
you live with yourselves?

00:09:02.308 --> 00:09:05.678
MAN #7: This is how it always starts.
First the building, then the whole block.

00:09:05.678 --> 00:09:07.313
MAN #8: They have no reason to
come to our place.

00:09:07.313 --> 00:09:08.181
More cops...

00:09:08.181 --> 00:09:09.482
MAN #7: Don't worry, they'll find one.

00:09:09.482 --> 00:09:13.253
Well, they don't sound Capped. I guess
that means I don't have to kill them.

00:09:13.253 --> 00:09:14.521
I need a gun.

00:09:14.521 --> 00:09:18.625
Well, Kleiner's here, so I guess I'll
hide out until his lackey gets off work

00:09:18.625 --> 00:09:20.226
then find out where he is,

00:09:20.226 --> 00:09:24.531
because it would've killed him to take
three seconds to give me an address.

00:09:24.531 --> 00:09:28.168
Nobody knows what they're doing.
I see THAT hasn't changed.

00:09:28.168 --> 00:09:30.303
Yeah, what was his name? Barney?

00:09:30.303 --> 00:09:35.175
I did find it kind of hilarious how
he's like, "It's me from Black Mesa."

00:09:35.175 --> 00:09:36.209
[lock buzzes]

00:09:36.209 --> 00:09:38.845
Dammit, not this way.

00:09:38.845 --> 00:09:43.616
I mean we had, what, 15,000
employees at that facility alone?

00:09:43.616 --> 00:09:47.120
He's talking like we're best
friends. I don't even remember him.

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:50.757
"It's me, Gordon, from General Electric."

00:09:50.757 --> 00:09:52.225
Oh, more cops.

00:09:53.326 --> 00:09:55.829
Great. I feel safer all ready.

00:09:55.829 --> 00:09:58.131
Maybe there's a roof access up here.

00:09:58.131 --> 00:09:59.098
METROCOP #5: Get moving.

00:09:59.098 --> 00:10:01.134
Oh. Hi.

00:10:01.134 --> 00:10:04.838
No go on the stairs. So now what?

00:10:06.272 --> 00:10:08.408
Man, fuck the CIA!

00:10:10.677 --> 00:10:13.480
You know what the problem is? We
didn't negotiate.

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:15.081
All I said was "Hawaii",

00:10:15.081 --> 00:10:19.052
but I would've taken Jamaica,
Cayman Islands, anything like that.

